<title>USA: FCC pegs US corn crop at 9.02 bln bu, soy 2.28 bln.</title>
<headline>FCC pegs US corn crop at 9.02 bln bu, soy 2.28 bln.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farmers Commodity Corp said on Tuesday it estimated 1996-97 U.S. corn production at 9.020 billion bushels and soybean output at 2.276 billion bushels.</p>
<p>FCC estimated the U.S. corn yield at 123.1 bushels per acre and the U.S. soybean yield at 35.88 bushels.</p>
<p>The U.S. Department of Agriculture on August 12 put U.S. corn production at 8.695 billion bushels and soybean output at 2.300 billion. USDA forecast a corn yield at 118.7 bushels and soybean yield of 36.2 bushels.</p>
<p>A month ago FCC forecast U.S. corn output at 9.081 billion and soybean production at 2.271 billion.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720</p>
</text>
